# Test: the filter subject names every attribute Ze advertises
# VALIDATES: AC-1 -- a route carrying ORIGIN, MULTI_EXIT_DISC, LOCAL_PREF,
#            ATOMIC_AGGREGATE and CLUSTER_LIST reaches an import filter with all
#            five named in FilterUpdateInput.Update.
# PREVENTS:  the five silent drops appendSingleAttr made for the life of the
#            function. Its type switch named a pointer form for each of the five,
#            and knownAttrParsers boxes the value form, so a Go type switch arm
#            that no producer can match dropped the attribute with nothing logged.
#            A filter asked to judge one of the five judged the route without it.
#
# Flow:
# 1. ze-peer sends one UPDATE over an IBGP session carrying all five attributes,
#    plus AS_PATH and NEXT_HOP, for 10.0.0.0/24.
# 2. The import chain calls filter-subject-test:record-subject.
# 3. The fixture plugin records FilterUpdateInput.Update and fails when any of
#    the five names is absent from it.
#
# The session is IBGP because LOCAL_PREF and CLUSTER_LIST belong on an internal
# session (RFC 4271 Section 5.1.5, RFC 4456 Section 8); an EBGP peer sending
# either is the case a receiver is entitled to discard.

# Source peer sends one route carrying all five attributes.
stdin=peer:terminator=EOF_PEER
option=tcp_connections:value=1
option=timeout:value=15s
# Marker(16) + Len=004F(79) + Type=02 + WdLen=0000 + AttrLen=0034(52)
#   ORIGIN:           40010102                      (incomplete)
#   AS_PATH:          40020A02020000FDE90000FDEA    (AS_SEQ [65001 65002])
#   NEXT_HOP:         4003040A000001                (10.0.0.1)
#   MULTI_EXIT_DISC:  80040400000064                (100)
#   LOCAL_PREF:       40050400000096                (150)
#   ATOMIC_AGGREGATE: 400600                        (no value)
#   CLUSTER_LIST:     800A080101010102020202        (1.1.1.1 2.2.2.2)
#   NLRI:             180A0000                      (10.0.0.0/24)
action=send:conn=1:seq=1:hex=FFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF004F02000000344001010240020A02020000FDE90000FDEA4003040A0000018004040000006440050400000096400600800A080101010102020202180A0000
EOF_PEER

# ze configuration: one external filter plugin on the import chain.
stdin=ze-bgp:terminator=EOF_CONF
plugin {
    external filter-subject-test {
        run "ze-test fixture plugin/filter-subject-names-every-attribute";
        encoder json;
    }
}
bgp {
    router-id 1.2.3.4;
    session {
        asn {
            local 65000
        }
    }
    filter {
        import [ filter-subject-test:record-subject ];
    }
    peer peer1 {
        connection {
            remote {
                ip 127.0.0.1
            }
            local {
                ip auto
                accept false
            }
        }
        session {
            asn {
                local 65000
                remote 65000
            }
            family {
                ipv4/unicast { prefix { maximum 10000; } }
            }
        }
    }
}
EOF_CONF

# Process orchestration
cmd=background:seq=1:exec=ze-peer --port $PORT:stdin=peer
cmd=foreground:seq=2:exec=ze -:stdin=ze-bgp:timeout=15s
expect=exit:code=0
# The subject the daemon handed the filter, printed by the fixture. Each name is
# asserted separately so a red says WHICH attribute is missing.
expect=stderr:pattern=OK: the subject names all five attributes
expect=stderr:pattern=origin incomplete
expect=stderr:pattern=med 100
expect=stderr:pattern=local-preference 150
expect=stderr:pattern=atomic-aggregate
expect=stderr:pattern=cluster-list 1.1.1.1 2.2.2.2
